# =============================================================================
# FRONTEND ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values before running the app.
#
# Variables are divided into two categories:
# - CLIENT-SIDE (NEXT_PUBLIC_*): Exposed to the browser, safe for non-sensitive config
# - SERVER-SIDE: Only accessible in API routes and server components, never sent to browser
#
# ⚠️  SECRET HANDLING: This file must only ever contain PLACEHOLDER values.
# Never commit real credentials. For the secret inventory (purpose, environment,
# owner, rotation cadence, revocation path) and the leak-response procedure
# (containment, rotation, verification), see SECURITY.md.

# =============================================================================
# CLIENT-SIDE VARIABLES (NEXT_PUBLIC_*)
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stellar Network Configuration (REQUIRED)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Stellar Soroban RPC URL for blockchain interaction
# Default: https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org

# Deployed FiatBridge contract address (starts with 'C')
# Default: CAWYXBN4PSVXD7NIYEWVFFIIIEUCC6PUN3IMG3J2WHKDB4NVIISMXBPR (testnet)
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIAT_BRIDGE_CONTRACT=CAWYXBN4PSVXD7NIYEWVFFIIIEUCC6PUN3IMG3J2WHKDB4NVIISMXBPR

# Native XLM Stellar Asset Contract (SAC) address
# Default: CDLZFC3SYJYDZT7K67VZ75HPJVIEUVNIXF47ZG2FB2RMQQVU2HHGCYSC (testnet)
NEXT_PUBLIC_XLM_SAC_CONTRACT=CDLZFC3SYJYDZT7K67VZ75HPJVIEUVNIXF47ZG2FB2RMQQVU2HHGCYSC

# Stellar Horizon URL for historical data and fallback queries (OPTIONAL)
# Only read by src/lib/stellarContract.ts:52
# Defaults to horizon-testnet or horizon.stellar.org based on RPC URL
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STELLAR_HORIZON_URL=https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI Assistant Configuration (OPTIONAL)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public Google Gemini API key for client-side AI features (OPTIONAL)
# If not set, falls back to server-side GEMINI_API_KEY
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Monitoring & Error Tracking (OPTIONAL)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sentry DSN for error tracking and monitoring (OPTIONAL)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://your_public_key@your_org.ingest.sentry.io/your_project_id

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feature Flags (OPTIONAL)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Enable specific features using NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_* variables
# Example: NEXT_PUBLIC_FLAG_NEW_FEATURE=true
# Check src/lib/featureFlags.ts for available flags

# --- App / API ---
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080
VITE_CHAIN_ID=1

# --- Wallet / RPC ---
VITE_RPC_URL=http://localhost:8545
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=

# Paystack secret key for payment processing (REQUIRED for withdrawals)
# Use a placeholder only — never commit a real key. See SECURITY.md for rotation.
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_paystack_secret_key_here

# Payout provider to use (DEFAULT: paystack)
PAYOUT_PROVIDER=paystack

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payout Field Encryption (REQUIRED for persisting payout data)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sensitive payout fields (bank account numbers, recipient identifiers) are
# encrypted at rest with an authenticated cipher (AES-256-GCM). Ciphertext is
# stored with a versioned key id so records can be re-encrypted during rotation.
#
# Keys MUST come from the configured secret-management boundary (e.g. your
# secrets manager / platform env injection). Never hardcode or commit real keys.
#
# PAYOUT_ENCRYPTION_KEYS: comma-separated list of "<keyId>:<base64-32-byte-key>"
# entries. The FIRST entry is the active key used for new writes; remaining
# entries are retained for decrypting older ciphertext during rotation.
# PAYOUT_ENCRYPTION_KEYS=v1:base64_32_byte_key_placeholder
#
# PAYOUT_ENCRYPTION_ACTIVE_KEY_ID: key id used for new encryptions (DEFAULT: first entry)
# PAYOUT_ENCRYPTION_ACTIVE_KEY_ID=v1
#
# PAYOUT_LOOKUP_HMAC_KEY: base64-encoded key for keyed-digest (HMAC-SHA256) lookup
# indexes over sensitive fields. Keyed digests allow equality lookup without
# storing plaintext, but they are deterministic: identical inputs yield identical
# digests, so they leak equality and are vulnerable if the key is compromised.
# Keep plaintext indexes to a minimum and prefer keyed digests only where lookup
# is required. Rotating this key requires rebuilding the lookup index.
# PAYOUT_LOOKUP_HMAC_KEY=base64_hmac_key_placeholder

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin Authentication & Security
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# API token for admin operations (OPTIONAL)
# Used to authenticate admin API requests
# ADMIN_API_TOKEN=your_admin_api_token_here

# Admin secret for reconciliation and audit log endpoints (OPTIONAL)
# ADMIN_SECRET=your_admin_secret_here

# Comma-separated list of IP addresses allowed for admin access (OPTIONAL)
# Example: ADMIN_IP_ALLOWLIST=203.0.113.10,198.51.100.20
# ADMIN_IP_ALLOWLIST=

# Bypass IP allowlist checks for localhost in development (DEFAULT: false)
# Only effective in development, ignored in production
# ADMIN_IP_ALLOWLIST_BYPASS_LOCAL=true

# Number of trusted proxy hops appended to X-Forwarded-For (DEFAULT: 0)
# Prefer platform client-IP headers; set this only when your proxy chain is trusted
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI Assistant (Server-Side)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Google Gemini API key for server-side AI features (OPTIONAL)
# Used in /api/ai/chat endpoint, never exposed to client
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build & Deployment Configuration (OPTIONAL)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sentry organization and project for release tracking (OPTIONAL)
# Used during build to upload source maps
# SENTRY_ORG=your_sentry_org
# SENTRY_PROJECT=your_sentry_project

# =============================================================================
# CONTENT SECURITY POLICY (CSP) & SECURITY HEADERS
# =============================================================================
# Issue #113: restrictive CSP + header baseline.
#
# CSP starts in REPORT-ONLY mode so violations can be triaged before enforcement.
# Set CSP_ENFORCE=true only after the report-only phase shows no unexpected
# violations in production browser tests.

# Toggle enforcement (DEFAULT: false = Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only)
# CSP_ENFORCE=false

# Endpoint that receives CSP violation reports (OPTIONAL)
# Defaults to /api/csp-report when unset
# CSP_REPORT_URI=/api/csp-report

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CSP ORIGIN INVENTORY (per environment)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Comma-separated allowlists consumed by the CSP builder. Each entry is a full
# origin (scheme + host + optional port). Wildcards are NOT supported.
#
# Adding a new third-party origin requires review (see SECURITY.md):
#   1. Confirm the origin is required and cannot be proxied server-side.
#   2. Add it to the correct directive below for the target environment.
#   3. Deploy in report-only mode, triage violations, then enforce.

# script-src: JS bundles, wallet SDKs, analytics
# CSP_SCRIPT_SRC=https://app.example.com

# connect-src: RPC, Horizon, wallet bridges, API, Sentry
# CSP_CONNECT_SRC=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org,https://horizon-testnet.stellar.org

# img-src: token icons, avatars, data/blob URIs
# CSP_IMG_SRC=https://app.example.com

# frame-src: wallet iframes / embedded providers
# CSP_FRAME_SRC=

# form-action: allowed form submission targets
# CSP_FORM_ACTION=https://app.example.com

# frame-ancestors: who may embed this app (DEFAULT: 'none')
# CSP_FRAME_ANCESTORS='none'

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECURITY HEADER BASELINE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Referrer-Policy (DEFAULT: strict-origin-when-cross-origin)
# CSP_REFERRER_POLICY=strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Permissions-Policy (DEFAULT: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=())
# CSP_PERMISSIONS_POLICY=camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# =============================================================================
# NOTES
# =============================================================================
# - Variables marked (REQUIRED) must be set for the app to function properly
# - Variables marked (OPTIONAL) have sensible defaults or are feature-specific
# - Variables marked (DEFAULT: value) will use the specified value if not set
# - See src/lib/env.ts for the Zod schemas that validate these variables
# - Secret inventory, rotation cadence, and leak response: see SECURITY.md
